          %h2#statement Statement
          %p
            Throughout, let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℋ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{H}
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/separable+Hilbert+space"} separable
            infinite-dimensional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+numbers"} complex
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilbert+space"} Hilbert space
          %p
          #KuiperTheorem.num_theorem
            %h6 Theorem
            %p
              %strong (Kuiper’s theorem)
              %br/
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+group"} topological
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitary+group"} unitary group
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/U%28%E2%84%8B%29"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℋ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{U}(\mathcal{H})
              in either the
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "UH#NormTopology"} norm topology
            %p or the equivalent
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a{:href => "UH#StrongOperatorTopology"} strong operator topology
              %li
                %p
                  %a{:href => "UH#WeakOperatorTopology"} weak operator topology
              %li
                %p
                  %a{:href => "UH#CompactOpenTopology"} compact-open topology
            %p
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contractible"} contractible
              in that there is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+homotopy"} left homotopy
              between the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity"} identity
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi id
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℋ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℋ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} id \;\colon\; U(\mathcal{H}) \to U(\mathcal{H})
              and the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constant+function"} constant function
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi const
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} e
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℋ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℋ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} const_{\mathrm{e}} \;\colon\; U(\mathcal{H}) \to U(\mathcal{H})
            %p
              Similarly, since the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/general+linear+group"} general linear group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℋ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL(\mathcal{H})
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bounded+operators"} bounded operators
              is homotopy-equivalent to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/U%28%E2%84%8B%29"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℋ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{U}(\mathcal{H})
              by the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gram-Schmidt+process"} Gram-Schmidt process
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contractible"} contractible
          %p
            See the commented list of references
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#References"} below
